@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+---
+id: task-005-implement-rfc-6902-json-patch-diff-createpatch
+type: task
+title: "Implement RFC 6902 JSON Patch diff createPatch"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document instead of the whole
+new version. Add a function that produces a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) describing the difference between
+two documents, so the existing `applyPatch` can turn one into the other without resending the whole
+document.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Exported `createPatch(from, to): JsonPatchOperation[]` from `src/index.ts`, implemented in
+  `src/jsonPatch.ts` alongside the existing `applyPatch`/`JsonPatchOperation` it shares types and a
+  `deepEqual` helper with.
+- Diff strategy, by the type of `from`/`to` at each JSON Pointer path:
+  - Equal values (by the existing deep-equality check) emit nothing.
+  - Two JSON objects recurse member-by-member: a member only in `from` is a `remove`, a member only
+    in `to` is an `add`, a member in both recurses into its own diff instead of replacing the whole
+    member.
+  - Two arrays are diffed with a longest-common-subsequence edit script (by deep equality of
+    elements), so insertions/removals anywhere in the array &mdash; not only at the tail &mdash;
+    produce localized `add`/`remove` ops instead of rewriting everything after the change. An
+    adjacent delete+insert at the same resulting index (an element that changed in place) is merged
+    into a single `replace` op. See dl-005 for why.
+  - Anything else (scalars, or a value that changed shape, e.g. object vs. array) is a single
+    `replace` at that path.
+- All values embedded in produced operations are `structuredClone`d, so the returned patch does not
+  alias into `from` or `to` and is unaffected by later mutation of either.
+- Added `escapeToken` to `src/jsonPointer.ts` (the inverse of its existing unescaping), used to build
+  member paths safely (e.g. a member literally named `a/b~c` round-trips through its escaped pointer
+  segment `a~1b~0c`).
+- Tests added to `src/jsonPatch.test.ts`: empty diff, single-member add/remove/replace, recursing
+  only into the changed branch of a nested object, pointer escaping, array add/remove/replace at the
+  tail and in the middle, whole-value replace on a shape change (object vs array, and at the root),
+  a combined round-trip case (`applyPatch(from, createPatch(from, to))` equals `to`), non-mutation of
+  both inputs, and that the returned patch is independent of later mutation of `to`.
+- `npm run typecheck` and `npm test` pass (95 tests, 0 failures).
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- None identified; `createPatch` and `applyPatch` are exact inverses for the documented diff
+  strategy, verified by the round-trip test.
